Mordain the Fleshweaver is an excoriate of [[House Phiarlan]] who was cast out after developing an obsessive, heretical study of flesh-warping magic. He resides in a tower known as [[Blackroot]] deep within the wilds of [[Droaam]].

Once a gifted member of House Phiarlan's Shadow Network, Mordain's research into Xoriat and the Daelkyr led him to grotesque experiments. The Twelve declared him excoriate and attempted to destroy him; he survived and retreated to Droaam. His tower is surrounded by his "children" — hybrid creatures he has sculpted from living flesh.

He is neither reliably hostile nor friendly. Mordain will trade information or services for something he cannot obtain himself, particularly specimens, rare texts, or access to planar phenomena.

!! Known Abilities
* Flesh-warping transmutation (Daelkyr-derived)
* Aberrant dragonmark (suspected)
* Extensive knowledge of Xoriat-influenced biology

!! Connections
* Formerly [[House Phiarlan]]
* Rumored contact with [[The Daughters of Sora Kell]]
* Has dealings with agents of [[The Emerald Claw]]
